# Shell scripts must keep LF line endings regardless of the checking-out
# machine's git config. core.autocrlf=true (the common Windows default)
# would otherwise convert them to CRLF on checkout - harmless for scripts
# only ever opened in an editor, but silently broken for any script that
# gets run directly (bash/sh) or mounted into a Linux container: a CRLF
# shebang line fails outright, and CRLF elsewhere leaves a stray \r on the
# end of shell variables (e.g. a password), so equality/auth checks that
# depend on it fail with no obvious cause.
*.sh text eol=lf
